     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi D-RUGies,<div><br></div><div>Just wanted to let you know our weekly work session is on for tomorrow at 10am, in the DSI (360 Shields). Bring your questions/work and enjoy the space.</div><div><br></div><div>I need to leave a bit earlier tomorrow, so will be heading out around 11:30, but folks are welcome to stay past that time.</div><div><br></div><div><u><b>NEW WEEKLY PACKAGE(s) OF THE WEEK UPDATE!</b></u></div><div><br></div><div>Additionally, I&#39;m going to try and start something that we&#39;ll call &quot;<b>Package(s) of the Week</b>&quot;. Currently there are <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Times;font-size:medium\"><b>11, 556</b> </span>packages on <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466715892000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0zaTNCmu3rP2UZDfHPfdW-\">CRAN</a>, and many more in Github repositories and elsewhere! Many times someone has a package that may do what you need, and while it&#39;s fun finding new packages, it can be a bit overwhelming to searching for them.</div><div><br></div><div>So, if you have a package you really enjoy using that&#39;s a hidden gem, or a fun new package you just discovered, etc., please send them my way! I&#39;d prefer to try to focus on the packages that are a bit outside of the core/popular packages folks use (i.e., tidyverse, lattice, etc), but happy to take whatever feedback you all have. Ultimately I just want a sentence or two about the package or how you use it, a link to the vignette, and call it good. Here&#39;s a google form we can use to compile all of these:</div><div><br></div><div><ul><li><a href=\"https://goo.gl/forms/VzzeldnaEOkNImJ73\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://goo.gl/forms/VzzeldnaEOkNImJ73&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466715893000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0zhYDwTwd_GNzdtqtiXdZO\">https://goo.gl/forms/VzzeldnaEOkNImJ73</a><br></li></ul><div><br></div><ul><li><b style=\"font-weight:bold\"><i>SPYvsSPY</i></b><span style=\"font-weight:normal\">: For this week, I&#39;ll mention a recent CRAN addition that catalogues data from all the Spy vs. Spy comics (from MAD Magazine). Sort of a fun dataset for statistical examples or just playing around with. It&#39;s on CRAN, and on github </span><a href=\"https://github.com/shabbychef/SPYvsSPY\" style=\"font-weight:normal\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/shabbychef/SPYvsSPY&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466715893000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3tjvRsMBXlXCNxOdL0oO-Q\">here</a>.</li></ul></div><div><div><br></div><div>Adios,<br></div><div>Ryan</div><div><br></div>-- <br><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br><span style=\"line-height:19px\"><font face=\"times new roman, serif\"><i><b><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;float:none;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);display:inline\"><span> </span></span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"></b></i></font></span><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><font size=\"1\"><i>&quot;When we try to pick out anything by itself, we find it hitched to everything else in the universe.&quot;<b><br>John Muir (My First Summer in the Sierra, 1911)</b></i></font></div><span style=\"line-height:19px\"><font face=\"times new roman, serif\"><i><b>-----------------------------------------------------</b></i></font></span></div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;line-height:19px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font face=\"times new roman, serif\"><div>Ryan Peek</div><div>PhD Candidate, Graduate Group in Ecology<br></div><div dir=\"ltr\">Center for Watershed Sciences, UC Davis</div></font></span><div style=\"font-family:arial;font-size:small;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"line-height:19px\"><div><b style=\"color:rgb(11,83,148);font-family:&quot;times new roman&quot;,serif\"><i><a href=\"http://ryanpeek.github.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://ryanpeek.github.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466715893000&amp;usg=AOvVaw16Cqx7WndKEk0GwbU6ypWW\">ryanpeek.github.io</a></i></b><br></div><div><b style=\"color:rgb(11,83,148);f